    https://github.com/vtavakkoli/QCeNN-MI

When publishing or releasing any project, software, documentation, or
product that incorporates or adapts the Covered Work, the licensee MUST
include this attribution in its public documentation, acknowledgments,
NOTICE, or another comparably visible place. Attribution must identify the
Covered Work and its authors and link to the original repository.

4. Mandatory citation of publicly reported research or results

Any scholarly paper, preprint, thesis, poster, public presentation,
technical report, public benchmark, or public dataset that materially
uses the Covered Work or reports results produced with it MUST include
a reference to the QCeNN-MI software, using the applicable citation
metadata in CITATION.cff or the following equivalent reference:

    V. Tavakkoli and K. Mohsenzadegan, "QCeNN-MI: Quantum Cellular
    Nonlinear Network for Matrix Inversion," software, 2026.
    https://github.com/vtavakkoli/QCeNN-MI

For works with a bibliography, include a conventional bibliographic
citation there. For other public material, a clearly visible written
credit and repository URL are sufficient. Citing related scientific
publications, including the referenced 2019 Sensors paper, is encouraged
where scientifically relevant but is separate from the required software
citation.

